# Vercel serves site/ and nothing else. Keeping the harvester out of the
# upload is what stops requirements.txt triggering Python runtime detection,
# and it keeps corpus.db (1.3 MB and growing) off the CDN entirely.
#
# Leading slashes matter: a bare "data/" would also exclude site/data/,
# which is the corpus the dashboard fetches.
/pipeline/
/tools/
/tests/
/sources/
/data/
/.github/
/_to_delete/
/requirements.txt
/taxonomy.yml
/README.md
